{{History of Balisca}}
The '''United Provinces of Bayara''' ({{langx|an|Provincias Unitas de Bayara|link=}}), earlier known as the '''United Provinces of the Marañón''' ({{langx|an|Las Provincias Unidas del Marañón|link=no}}), was a name adopted in 1743 by the [[Congress of San Agustín]] for the territory of the [[Xacano concession]] that exercised sovereignty following the outbreak of the [[Volisanian Civil War]], which marked the beginning of the [[Volisanya Boba]] period. 

